[Event "Winning paths and distant opposition"]
[ChapterName "Finish from the opposition"]
[Orientation "white"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "3k4/8/3K4/3P4/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1"]

{ [%ts 9:49] White just played Kd6: kings on the same file, one square between them, Black to move. Black would love to pass, but he can't. Now finish the job. }
1... Ke8 { [%ts 9:57] Black has to give way, to e8 or c8. Either way, White goes to the other side. }
( 1... Kc8 { [%ts 10:05] If Black goes to c8 instead, the white king goes to the other side. } 2. Ke7 $1 { [%ts 10:05] Ke7, covering d7 and d8. } ( 2. Ke6 { Also wins by the engine, but it lets Black back in front of the pawn. Go to the other side. } ) ( 2. Kc6 { Also wins by the engine, but it lets Black back in front of the pawn. Go to the other side. } ) 2... Kc7 3. d6+ ( 3. Ke6 { Also wins by the engine, but it gives Black time. John finishes the job directly. } ) 3... Kc8 4. d7+ ( 4. Ke8 { Also wins by the engine, but it gives Black time. John finishes the job directly. } ) ( 4. Ke6 { Also wins by the engine, but it gives Black time. John finishes the job directly. } ) 4... Kc7 5. d8=Q+ ( 5. d8=R { Also wins, but take the queen. } ) ( 5. Ke8 { Also wins by the engine, but it gives Black time. John finishes the job directly. } ) )
2. Kc7 $1 { [%ts 10:05] The king goes to the other side, c7, and covers d7 and d8. }
( 2. Ke6 { Also wins by the engine, but it lets Black back in front of the pawn. Go to the other side. } ) ( 2. Kc6 { Also wins by the engine, but it lets Black back in front of the pawn. Go to the other side. } ) 
2... Ke7
3. d6+ $1 { [%ts 10:13] The pawn can march now: d6 check. }
( 3. Kc6 { Also wins by the engine, but it gives Black time. John finishes the job directly. } ) 
3... Ke8
4. d7+ $1
( 4. Kc8 { Also wins by the engine, but it gives Black time. John finishes the job directly. } ) ( 4. Kc6 { Also wins by the engine, but it gives Black time. John finishes the job directly. } ) 
4... Ke7
5. d8=Q+ $1 { [%ts 10:22] White promotes, gets a queen and wins. If White knows the opposition, nothing Black does from the start would have saved him once White played Kd3. }
( 5. d8=R { Also wins, but take the queen. } ) ( 5. Kc8 { Also wins by the engine, but it gives Black time. John finishes the job directly. } ) 
